-- The ramified columns: for each prime w of E dividing π a central unit
-- ν_w (an integral norm-one finite adele, 1 away from w and w̄, whose
-- w-component generates the units modulo w), the translation z_w of the
-- columns by the scalar ν_w, the ramifying operator ∏_{w∈s}(1 − z_w) and
-- its range, the ramified columns; short forms; the dimension bounds and
-- the spanning by short ramified columns.
-- Source: grh-compact/src/New/Columns/ChainValuation.lean ("Short integral
-- algebraic forms span; ramified columns have nearly full dimension.";
-- IsShort, Data.exists_centralGen, Data.centralGen, Data.centralRep,
-- Data.ramifyingOp, Data.ramifiedColumns, exists_eq_sub_centralGen,
-- sum_height_mul_kappa_le, finrank_ker_one_sub_centralGen_le,
-- ramifyingOp_finrank_comap_and_short, span_short_ramifiedColumns,
-- norm_star_piG_le_one).
-- Encoding. The source chooses ν_w by exists_centralGen (Data.centralGen);
-- here the family w ↦ ν_w is the field centralGen of the record of
-- choices (AutoChoices), bound by CentralGens, the property it is chosen
-- by. The scalar of ∏_{w∈T} ν_w is a product in the unit group of 𝔸_f(E),
-- and ∏_{w∈s}(1 − z_w) is written out as Σ_{T⊆s} (−1)^{|T|} z_T. Not
-- stated here: the determinant theta periods (detKernel, detPeriod,
-- detPeriod_eq_stdClassSum_sum, detPeriod_insert: θ_{α,α} of the pair
-- (I_n, I_n) of Lib/Weil), the general span_isShort_eq_top
-- (shortBasisConst of Lib/Adelic), and the good finite data and chains
-- (pairTranslates, admissibleTranslations, IsGoodDatum,
-- exists_chain_eq_sum, IsGoodDatum.gaugeLe_chain: the chains of lift
-- kernels of New/Seesaw and New/Rows).
-- Part of the GRH blueprint (layer 5, the argument).
